      "blocks": {
        "faq_zdMmcJ": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "What is an electrolyte powder and do I actually need one?",
            "answer": "<p>An electrolyte powder is a supplement that replaces minerals lost through sweat, heat, illness, or daily activity. It contains sodium, potassium, magnesium, and calcium, minerals that maintain fluid balance, nerve transmission, and muscle function. If you train, travel, sweat, or drink coffee, water alone is not putting those minerals back.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "faq_jcRQRR": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "How is Reevë different from a typical electrolyte drink mix?",
            "answer": "<p>Most electrolyte drink mixes cover two or three minerals. Reevë covers six, in the ratio your body actually loses them, and adds collagen peptides and real coconut water on top, at 8 calories and zero added sugar. See the full comparison table above for the category-by-category breakdown.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_wzn8BN": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "How do I use Reevë, and how many sticks a day is normal?",
            "answer": "<p>Mix one stick pack with 16 to 32 oz of water, depending on taste preference. Shake or stir until dissolved. Most people do 1 to 2 sticks a day, and 2 to 3 on hot days, during intense training, travel, or illness recovery. Listen to your body.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_Wp4geC": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "Does Reevë contain caffeine?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Reevë is caffeine-free, just clean hydration you can drink any time of day without affecting sleep or stacking on top of your usual coffee.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_TN4YxY": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "Why does Reevë taste different from other electrolyte powders?",
            "answer": "<p>No artificial flavors and no sucralose aftertaste. Sweetness comes entirely from monk fruit extract, so the finish is clean rather than syrupy, and the coconut water base gives it a naturally rounder mouthfeel than a citric-acid-only powder.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_zXxP3B": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "General",
            "question": "Can I mix Reevë into sparkling water or a smoothie?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Reevë dissolves cleanly in still or sparkling water, and works just as well stirred into a smoothie for an electrolyte and collagen boost.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_fTygbh": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Training & recovery",
            "question": "Is Reevë good as a pre-workout or post-workout electrolyte powder?",
            "answer": "<p>Both. Sip before training to pre-load sodium and magnesium, mid-session to stay ahead of cramping, and after to replace what sweat took and support recovery with collagen peptides. It is caffeine-free, so it will not interfere with pre-workout stimulants you already use.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_kchKb4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Training & recovery",
            "question": "Will Reevë help with muscle cramps and soreness?",
            "answer": "<p>Cramping is frequently linked to low sodium, potassium, magnesium, or calcium, exactly the four minerals a typical sports drink skips or under-doses. Reevë replaces all six electrolytes together, which is the combination most associated with reduced cramping in hard training.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_yCw4Gf": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Training & recovery",
            "question": "Is Reevë suitable for runners, cyclists, and endurance athletes?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Reevë is built for anyone who needs rapid electrolyte replenishment and collagen support for joint recovery, from casual gym-goers to long-distance runners and cyclists logging heavy mileage.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_HzQpUL": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Training & recovery",
            "question": "Can I use Reevë for recovery after a hangover or a long night out?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Dehydration and depleted electrolytes are a large part of what makes the morning after feel rough. One or two sticks with plenty of water is a common recovery-morning ritual for exactly that reason.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_nyXJDV": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Travel & on-the-go",
            "question": "Why is Reevë a good electrolyte drink mix for travelers?",
            "answer": "<p>Cabin air, time zone changes, and long layovers all dehydrate you faster than you notice. A stick pack weighs almost nothing, needs no refrigeration, and turns any bottle of water, at the gate, on the plane, or in a hotel room, into a full hydration reset.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
